On Tue, 18 Apr 2000, SRV wrote:

> And I have 3 choices from my local computer retailer:
> 1.- SB AWE 128 pci card
> 2.- SB PCI 128 Ensoniq chipset ct4810
> 3.- SB 512 PCI

>  Which one has better support in Linux?
> I am avoiding the SB Live, since the drivers are alpha and has some bugs.
> Apparently the SB 512 uses the same emu10k chipset as the SB Live?

Yes... the SBPCI512 uses the same chipset as the Live!.  Therefore it uses
the same driver and has the same bugs as the Live!.  If you've already
decided to stay away from the SB Live!, then you should stay away from the
PCI512.

Althoug... I'm using a PCI512 and I really don't have too many complaints.
The MIDI doesn't work on it, but I make my music with real instruments, so
it doesn't bother me at all.

-Paco
